# =============================================================================
# TerraPulse Egypt - Cloud Telemetry Database Configuration (Supabase)
# =============================================================================
#
# TerraPulse runs with zero configuration using embedded NASA satellite datasets
# and local clinician seed surveys. The statistical engine, charts, Leaflet and the
# choropleth polygons all work with no network. Three things still need internet:
#   1. ArcGIS basemap tiles from server.arcgisonline.com - without them the map
#      renders its polygons, markers and charts on a grid background, never an error.
#   2. Cairo/Inter webfonts from fonts.googleapis.com - system-font fallback offline.
#   3. The Supabase project below, but only when it is configured.
# TerraPulse is therefore "core-data offline", not "fully offline".
#
# To enable real-time crowdsourcing across multiple devices and clinics,
# copy this file to .env and configure your Supabase Project keys:
#
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Open the SQL Editor and run the script in
#    supabase/migrations/0001_init_physician_reports.sql
#    (the same text is shown verbatim in the app's "Cloud Database Sync" dialog).
# 3. Paste your Project URL and the client ("anon" / "publishable") API key below.
#
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY are accepted interchangeably:
# Supabase renamed the same browser-safe value, and the two dashboards label it
# differently. Set one, not both.
#
# This key is a PUBLIC client-side key: it is shipped in the built bundle and is not a
# secret. It only grants what Row Level Security allows, and the migration defines that
# narrowly - anon may INSERT a validated report and nothing else. It cannot SELECT, so
# no visitor can read another physician's submission; the feed therefore shows the local
# device's reports plus the embedded seed, and the status badge says "cloud submits
# allowed, reads blocked". A cross-device feed needs Supabase Auth and a read policy,
# which is a decision about disclosing migration intent, not a config flag.
#
# Do NOT put a service-role / secret key here (sb_secret_..., or a legacy JWT whose
# payload says "role": "service_role"). It bypasses RLS entirely and Vite inlines any
# VITE_* value into the public bundle. dbService refuses to use or store such a key.
#
# Both values can also be entered at runtime in the "Cloud Database Sync" dialog
# instead of being baked into .env.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-public-key
